.TH STONE 6.SH NAMEstone \- the game of stones.SH SYNOPSIS\fBstone\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONA take-away game against the computer.  It offers the rules, then asksfor the size of the pile (an odd number), whether the winner is theplayer who ends with an even or an odd number of stones (0 or 1), andthe most that may be taken in one turn.  You and the computer then takestones in turn until the pile is gone..SH FILES.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/SNOBOL/PHRASE.SYN\fRthe phrases it talks in..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fROne of Robert Heller's programs translated from SNOBOL4 into C, fromJames F. Gimpel's\fIAlgorithms in SNOBOL4\fR;\fR\fBDOC/snobol\fRdescribes the set and\fBSRC/effo_snobol\fRholds the source..SH SEE ALSOblackjak, poker